# The requirement-to-evidence table's scope for v0 (T-024-09; read by `evidence-table`).
#
# One row for every requirement, invariant, acceptance criterion, non-functional requirement and guarantee that
# SPEC.md defines and has not withdrawn:
#
#   ID | class | citations | note
#
# Classes. `m3`: needs a passing test whose `// verifies:` comment names it. `partly`: M3's, not met yet; cites the
# form item it waits on (`form:<item>`). `inspect`: M3's, verified by inspection; cites a check (`check:documentation`,
# `check:boundary`, `check:licence`) or a recorded review (`review:F-0NN`, whose notes must exist). `m4`: cites its
# feature and PLAN.md's 7.1 row for the family (`F-030 7.1:REQ-OPS`). `deferred`: cites the decision (`DEC-n`), or the
# assumption and risk (`ASM-1 6.2:risk-9`), or the feature and 7.1 row (`F-052 7.1:REQ-EXT`) that defers it.
# An `m3` row may cite `later-part:F-0NN`, the owner of a half that comes later.
#
# The switch below: only the CI step that passes `--ci` reads it; `--strict` on the command line always runs
# strictly. It only ever turns on: a head that reads `off` against a develop that reads `on` fails. T-024-10 sets
# it to `on` and changes no other line of this file.
#
# Moving an m3 row to m4 or deferred needs the PLAN.md rows it cites to have changed to place it there, as the
# ratchet in `evidence-table` checks against develop.

strict: off


